<BaseLayout
  title="How to Buy on Rakuten Ichiba — Rakuten Shopping Lab"
  description="A short guide for international shoppers: creating a Rakuten account, reading prices, shipping from Japan, and paying on Rakuten Ichiba."
  lang="en"
>
  <h1>How to Buy on Rakuten Ichiba</h1>
  <p>
    Rakuten Ichiba is one of Japan's largest online marketplaces, made up of
    thousands of independent shops. This site introduces products from its
    rankings. If you live outside Japan, here is the basics of how buying works.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Create a Rakuten account</h2>
  <p>
    You need a free Rakuten account to place an order. Registration is
    available in English: you can sign up with your email address from
    Rakuten's registration page and use the same account across Rakuten
    services.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Search and check the price</h2>
  <p>
    Prices on Rakuten Ichiba are shown in Japanese yen (JPY). In most cases the
    displayed price already includes consumption tax, but shipping is often
    charged separately — check each product page for the shipping fee and
    whether the shop offers free shipping above a certain amount. Product
    names and descriptions are usually in Japanese, so a browser translation
    tool can help.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Shipping: domestic by default</h2>
  <p>
    Many shops on Rakuten Ichiba ship only within Japan. If you live outside
    Japan, the common approach is to have your order delivered to a forwarding
    service in Japan and forwarded to your address — Rakuten's own forwarding
    service is called Rakuten Global Express. Fees and delivery times depend
    on the service and destination, so check before ordering. A smaller number
    of shops offer direct international shipping.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Payment</h2>
  <p>
    Many shops accept major international credit cards, but payment methods
    vary from shop to shop. Check the accepted payment methods on the shop or
    product page before you order. Your card issuer handles the currency
    conversion from yen.
  </p>

  <h2>5. About the links on this site</h2>
  <p>
    Product links on Rakuten Shopping Lab are Rakuten Affiliate Program links.
    If you buy through them, we may earn a commission from Rakuten — it does
    not change the price you pay. Prices and availability on this site are as
    checked when each article was published and may have changed; the product
    page on Rakuten Ichiba is always the source of truth.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
